# `.env.default` — environment floor committed and loaded by `bin/` wrappers and `.envrc`.
# This file is sourced by bash; keep it free of secrets and real credentials.
# Override values locally in `.env` (gitignored) or `.envrc.local` (gitignored).
#
# Recognized variables (defaults apply when unset):
#   LOG_LEVEL          debug | info | warning | error | critical   (default: info)
#   APP_ENV            development | test | production             (default: production)
#   API_HOST           bind address for the HTTP surface           (default: 127.0.0.1)
#   API_PORT           port for the HTTP surface                   (default: 8100)
#   HELLO_WORLD_NAME   default name for the CLI command            (default: world)
